PVD("poland_vision_2025-2050",{"docs":["","Poland National Development Concept 2050"],"s":{"1":[[1,"2","2","Strategic Planning and Future Scenarios Tools","it is necessary to prepare strategic planning tools aimed at exploring the consequences of ongoing changes and outlining potential future scenarios, and, at the same time, allowing public policies to be formulated in advance",""],[1,"3","8","Adaptive Strategic Planning and Decision-Making","Such an approach allows harnessing new opportunities by altering the objectives, actions or practices.",""],[1,"3","14","Operationalisation of the Development Management System of Poland","The consortium implementedthe GOSPOSTRATEG-III/0032/2020 project entitled: Operationalisation of the Development Management System of Poland.",""],[1,"4","8","Participatory Planning and Stakeholder Dialogue Mechanism","Participatory planning and consensus-seeking enables the NCR to be a \"balanced aggregate\" of diverse expectations, interests and solution ideas of the respective parties to the dialogue.",""],[1,"4","10","National Development Concept Updating Mechanism","will be updated whenever any significant changes in development trends occur in the country or worldwide.",""],[1,"14","9","Development Opportunity and Threat Early Identification Mechanism","early identification of opportunities and threats to development",""],[1,"17","1","National Scenario Planning and Implications Analysis","requires identifying a number of different plausible scenarios and exploring what implications they may have.",""],[1,"18","7","Strategic Foresight in Administration and the Economy","a wider use of strategic foresight in the administration and economy",""],[1,"22","13","AI-Supported Strategic and Operational Planning","developing strategic and operational plans to be subsequently implemented by external actors",""],[1,"29","1","Anticipatory Support Systems Reform","An anticipatory change in various support systems",""],[1,"29","1","Generation-Sensitive Cross-Sectoral Reforms","all future reforms in the areas of education, health care, housing and the labour market must also take into account the perspective and expectations of the current and next generations",""],[1,"21","7","Socialisation of Public Decision-Making","Increased socialisation of public decision-making has also been introduced",""],[1,"21","8","Participatory Local Community Project Implementation","the implementation of specific projects for local communities with stakeholder involvement, including deliberations, citizen panels and consultations",""],[1,"21","8","Public Administration Specialist Staffing Strengthening","the staffing of public administration (highly qualified specialists) was strengthened",""],[1,"43","2","Digital Public Administration Service Improvement","In public administration, the use of digital technologies can contribute to increasing the efficiency and quality of services provided by that sector, leading to greater citizen satisfaction.",""],[1,"47","34","Renewal of Crisis Management Strategic Objectives","to renew strategic objectives in this regard.",""],[1,"48","7","Monitoring and Warning Systems","monitoring and warning systems.",""],[1,"51","4","Strategic Planning and Public Management Improvement","improve strategic planning and public management methods",""],[1,"51","4","Reliable Public and Private Sector Data Provision","an increasingly reliable provision of data (e.g. big data from the public and private sectors)",""],[1,"51","4","Digital Twin Management and Simulation Tools","new management tools (e.g. digital twin and the related simulations of specific processes and investments in the virtual world)",""],[1,"51","4","Strategic Foresight Methods","strategic foresight methods",""],[1,"51","6","Public Data Collection and Sharing System Strengthening","strengthen the public data collection and sharing system (data-driven governance)",""],[1,"51","7","Strategic Foresight Methods Promotion","Promotion of the use of strategic foresight methods",""],[1,"51","8","Innovative Development Strategy Solutions","design new out-of-the-box and ground-breaking solutions that might be trivialised or overlooked during traditional preparation of development strategies",""],[1,"64","4","Forward-Looking Governance and Anticipation Model","introduction of a new model of forward-looking thinking that enables continuous and objective anticipation and evaluation of opportunities for and threats to the country's development",""],[1,"64","4","Integrated Public and Private Data System","integration and improvement of the system for collecting, analysing and interpreting data from public and private sources in order to provide a comprehensive picture of the country's situation",""],[1,"68","12","Trend Analysis for Strategic Decision-Making","using this knowledge to make decisions and formulate strategies.",""],[1,"65","8","Development and Public Finance Management Mechanisms","creation of mechanisms for development and public finance management",""],[1,"65","9","Transparent Strategic Finance System","ensuring transparency of the financing of strategic objectives and development priorities",""]],"2":[[1,"25","10","Housing Policy Reform","reformulate the existing housing",""],[1,"28","3","Affordable Housing Access and Tenure Policy","The state’s housing policy should offer a choice between ownership of a dwelling and secure rental so that access to affordable housing with decent living conditions is guaranteed as a fundamental human right.",""],[1,"28","3","Sustainable and Inclusive Housing Construction Standards","It is important that the construction of the housing stock is compliant with the principles of spatial order, universal design and takes into account energy and water conservation.",""],[1,"28","3","Housing Market Regulation and Anti-Speculation Measures","At the same time, the state should have a strong influence on the rules of the housing sector and the ability to limit and prevent the negative effects of free market mechanisms.",""],[1,"28","3","Social and Communal Housing Development Support","The state should become involved where the free market does not provide the adequate supply of housing stock – social and communal housing in particular needs to be developed and supported.",""],[1,"28","3","Vacant Property Conversion for Accessible Housing","The process of creating accessible housing stock should also take into account vacancies and unused office buildings, in the development of which social economy actors should play an important role.",""],[1,"28","3","Accessible Energy-Efficient Housing Standard","It is also important to apply a housing standard that will include architectural accessibility, low emission and energy efficiency as well as availability of goods and services and opportunities to participate in social and public life.",""],[1,"21","2","Local Government Social Housing for Long-Term Rental","A system of social housing for long-term rental, managed by local government units, was also developed.",""],[1,"33","3","Housing Stock Development and Revitalisation","development of the housing stock (construction of dwellings, adaptation of vacancies, revitalisation of",""],[1,"33","4","Residential Building Adaptation for Older Persons","adaptation of residential buildings to the needs of the elderly",""],[1,"59","6","Affordable Housing Provision","providing them with cheaper housing",""]],"3":[[1,"7","27","Long-Term Energy Policy Monitoring and Reform","long-term monitoring and reforms concerning energy policy",""],[1,"14","10","Energy Storage Technology Deployment","use of latest energy storage technologies",""],[1,"14","10","Smart Energy Infrastructure Deployment","deployment of smart energy infrastructure",""],[1,"14","10","Distributed Zero-Emission and Prosumer Energy System","The system is based on a model of distributed, diversified zero-emission sources with a significant share of prosumer energy.",""],[1,"18","7","Clean Energy Generation and Storage Investment","investments in reliable sources of energy generation (nuclear power), storage and use of alternative energy sources (RES, hydrogen)",""],[1,"18","7","Energy Efficiency Improvement Programme","increased energy efficiency (also in transport)",""],[1,"20","14","Energy Efficiency Improvement Programme","improve energy efficiency",""],[1,"19","16","Alternative Energy Generation and Storage Investment Programme","The pursuit of energy security resulted in legislative and investment solutions fostering the generation, storage and use of energy from alternative sources such as RES, distributed energy, as well as nuclear energy (including small modular reactors, the so-called SMRs) or fusion power.",""],[1,"20","14","Domestic Energy Resource Utilisation Measures","increase the use of domestic energy resources",""],[1,"20","14","Nuclear Power Development","develop nuclear power",""],[1,"20","14","Renewable Energy Development","develop nuclear power and RES",""],[1,"20","14","Biogas Utilisation Expansion","increase the role of biogas",""],[1,"20","14","Energy Storage Expansion","expand energy storage",""],[1,"20","14","Hydrogen Energy Utilisation","increase the use of hydrogen",""],[1,"20","14","Energy Resource Recovery Measures","recover energy resources",""],[1,"20","14","Comprehensive Building Thermo-Modernisation","most of the buildings underwent deep and comprehensive thermo-modernisation",""],[1,"20","14","Smart Metering and Dynamic Tariff Mechanism","Peak-hour electricity consumption was also reduced by means of smart metering and new dynamic tariffs",""],[1,"20","18","Renewable Energy Share Investment Projects","projects aimed at increasing the RES share in the system",""],[1,"34","15","Economy-Wide Energy Reform for Climate Neutrality","Energy reforms must systemically address all sectors of the economy.",""],[1,"34","16","Energy Generation Decentralisation and Diversification","changing the structure of energy generation through decentralisation and diversification of generation sources based on sustainable use of largely renewable resources.",""],[1,"35","5","Energy System Modernisation","It is therefore necessary to modernise the energy system",""],[1,"35","5","Smart Energy Technology Deployment","to make greater use of the constantly evolving modern, smart technologies for the generation, transmission, distribution and storage of energy",""],[1,"35","5","Energy Market Structure Reform","It is critical to build a new structure of the energy market components (taking into account Poland's participation in the international energy market) that will induce a shift away from centralised large-scale fossil-based energy and bring the sector closer to the European model",""],[1,"35","6","Civic Energy and Local Energy Cooperatives Support","support for civic energy based on the model of development of energy democracy that is independent of large power generation units",""],[1,"35","7","Distributed and Prosumer Energy Generation Development","The development of such energy generation will also contribute to the eradication of energy poverty and will be part of the implementation of a human right of access to energy.",""],[1,"35","7","Comprehensive Building Energy Efficiency Renovation","These measures should be accompanied by improvements in energy efficiency of buildings, ideally in a comprehensive renovation formula.",""],[1,"49","6","Climate-Resilient Energy Market Architecture","Building the new and maintaining the existing energy market architecture will require ensuring that it is resilient to the effects of climate change",""],[1,"57","6","Urban Energy Production and Storage Infrastructure","urban areas should be saturated with infrastructure for energy production and storage",""],[1,"62","6","Distributed Renewable Energy Technology Development","The energy transformation and further development of technologies based on distributed, renewable energy sources can provide a major boost to rural development.",""],[1,"63","2","Rural Renewable Energy Infrastructure Development","development of renewable energy infrastructure",""],[1,"64","9","Sustainable Energy System and Efficiency Programme","ensuring a stable, efficient and sustainable energy system, diversifying energy sources and improving energy efficiency",""],[1,"65","4","Energy Transformation Programme","energy transformation, so that the state's energy security is enhanced and convenient and fair development conditions are created for local communities",""],[1,"68","10","Prosumer Energy Generation","energy generation by local communities, energy co-operatives or associations working to reduce dependence on fossil fuels, reduce greenhouse gas emissions and create local sources of sustainable energy.",""]],"4":[[1,"14","9","Circular Economy Implementation in Agriculture","implementation of the circular economy in agriculture",""],[1,"15","7","Circular Economy Implementation","implementation of the circular economy",""],[1,"19","16","Moderate Economy Solutions for Sustainable Consumption","The awareness of the major impact of consumption on the natural environment, the availability of raw materials and the exploitation of space led to the development of a consensus and the introduction of a number of moderate economy solutions.",""],[1,"20","12","Food Waste Prevention Programmes","Food waste prevention programmes were initiated",""],[1,"20","17","Sustainable Consumption Cost-Linkage Policy","A strong link between costs and consumption was established.",""],[1,"20","18","Sustainable Public Procurement Implementation","implementing sustainable public procurement",""],[1,"20","18","Low-Emission Elimination Programme","The programme for systematic elimination of low emissions was expanded significantly.",""],[1,"36","8","Cross-Sectoral Environmental Pressure Reduction","It is necessary to reduce the pressure of the energy, transport and construction sectors on the environment",""],[1,"36","11","Circular Economy and Resource Efficiency Measures","Such a resource-efficient and low-emission management practice is based on a circular economy where resources circulate through successive cycles of production and consumption and waste generation is minimised.",""],[1,"36","11","Circular Economy Enabling Solutions","Implementation and preservation of a moderate economy requires technological, organisational, legal and fiscal solutions that will enable development of new operational mechanisms for the economy",""],[1,"21","17","Environmental Cost Integration in Development Planning","Environmental costs became an integral part of the country’s development planning",""],[1,"36","11","Environmental Cost and Ecosystem Valuation Integration","These solutions should take into account environmental costs, integrate the valuation of ecosystem services into development planning and decision-making processes",""],[1,"21","17","Environmental Resource Rationing Schemes","The existing environmental resources were identified and brought under partial rationing schemes",""],[1,"43","2","Natural Resource Restoration and Resource Efficiency Initiative","technological acceleration should contribute to the restoration of natural resources, e.g. by making the economy more resource-efficient (e.g. in terms of water consumption) or by increasing the uptake of greenhouse gases by ecosystems.",""],[1,"43","2","Real-Time Environmental Monitoring and Pollution Control System","Modern solutions for real-time environmental monitoring and analysis of spatial environmental data should be used for more effective pollution prevention and control.",""],[1,"37","6","Sustainable Fertiliser and Plant Protection Use","reasonable use of fertilisers and plant protection products",""],[1,"44","11","Degraded Land Reclamation and Rehabilitation","reclamation or (where feasible and environmentally sound) rehabilitation of degraded land",""],[1,"47","27","Rare Earth Metals Access Initiative","to ensure access to the shrinking deposits of rare earth metals which are located",""],[1,"50","6","Circular Economy and Sustainable Environment Policy","The strategic orientation of the economy towards the circular model and a sustainable environment",""],[1,"64","6","Public Policy Principles Reform for Sustainable Resource Use","changing the fundamental principles and approaches used in the formulation and implementation of public policies so that they can make a real contribution to generationally, socially and environmentally fair use of resources and are not focused solely on GDP growth",""],[1,"64","6","Natural Environment and Spatial Resource Mainstreaming","raising the natural environment and space to the status of critical resources in all areas of life and decision-making",""],[1,"64","7","Resource Efficiency and Emissions Reduction","sustainable implementation of moderate use of resources, reduction of the environmental pressure, including specifically limitation of greenhouse gas emissions, in industry, agriculture, transport and construction",""],[1,"64","7","Public Awareness and Responsible Consumption Promotion","increased public awareness of the impact on the planet and promotion of responsible consumption",""],[1,"70","5","Local Food Supply and Short Transport Chains","It is characterised by minimising the use of long transport routes, which translates into lower environmental impact, fresher products and support for local economies and communities.",""]],"5":[[1,"15","3","Protected Areas Expansion Programme","The extent of protected areas, including those under strict protection, has been increased.",""],[1,"15","3","Priority Ecosystem and Species Protection Support","The protection of wetlands, forest ecosystems and endangered species is specially supported.",""],[1,"15","3","River and Wetland Ecosystem Restoration Programmes","River renaturalisation, wetland and peatland reclamation and floodplain ecosystem rehabilitation programmes have been implemented.",""],[1,"15","3","Ecological Corridor Network Coherence Initiative","The coherence of the ecological corridor network is ensured.",""],[1,"20","17","Protected Areas and National Parks Expansion","A decision was made to increase the space of protected areas, including through the establishment of new national parks.",""],[1,"20","17","Forest Tax Rate Increase","Mechanisms were put in place to support local communities through e.g. ... increased forest tax rates.",""],[1,"20","17","Wetland Floodplain and Ecological Corridor Conservation Regulations","New conservation regulations included, among others, increased protection of wetlands, natural floodplains and ecological corridors.",""],[1,"21","17","Restoration of Degraded Environmental Assets","the most degraded assets subjected to restoration",""],[1,"39","2","Sustainable and Regenerative Agriculture Programme","it is imperative to promote sustainable and regenerative agriculture that ensures food security.",""],[1,"39","2","Climate-Adapted Agricultural Species and Varieties","it will be important that the species and varieties used in agricultural production are adapted to changing climatic conditions",""],[1,"39","2","Sustainable Livestock Farming and Animal Welfare","livestock farming is sustainable and ensures animal welfare.",""],[1,"39","2","Agricultural Technology Modernisation Support","it is essential to support agriculture in the use of new technologies - robotisation, automation and digitalisation of food production processes",""],[1,"39","2","Rural Economic Diversification and Sustainability Support","it will also be important to support rural areas in developing entrepreneurship, crafts, food production for local markets, farming-related services, renewable energy production, biodiversity enhancement and eco-tourism.",""],[1,"39","5","Blue and Green Infrastructure Network Development","Development of a coherent network of blue and green infrastructure, including the sustainable protection of naturally valuable areas, especially aquatic and forest ecosystems",""],[1,"39","5","Open Space Protection Measure","It is necessary to safeguard open spaces effectively",""],[1,"39","5","Protected-Area Community Support Initiative","to support local communities in protected areas to strengthen their commitment to nature conservation",""],[1,"40","3","Ecological Corridor Protection Programme","This requires shaping and protecting ecological corridors at European, national, regional and local levels.",""],[1,"40","3","Natural Habitat and Ecological Corridor Restoration","Preserving and restoring good quality natural habitats and ecological corridors is a prerequisite for protecting biodiversity and stopping the extinction of species.",""],[1,"40","3","Pollinating Insect Population Recovery Programme","It is necessary to reverse the decline in the number of pollinating insects and to ensure growth of their populations until they reach a satisfactory level that will provide for the conservation of the species and increased resilience of ecosystems.",""],[1,"41","1","Invasive Alien Species Prevention and Monitoring","it is necessary to prevent and monitor the spread of invasive alien species",""],[1,"41","1","Sustainable Forest Management","Implementation of sustainable forest management counteracting the impoverishment of forests and promoting the management of Polish forests will ensure the preservation of their multifunctional character for the present and future generations",""],[1,"37","7","Sustainable Marine Area Planning and Management","There is also a need for for sustainable planning and management in marine areas that will combine the protection and restoration of marine ecosystems and resources with their reasonable use (e.g. as regards fishing, installing cyber networks and building energy infrastructure).",""],[1,"20","12","Regenerative Agriculture Development Support","support was provided to the development of regenerative agriculture",""],[1,"42","7","Agricultural Robotisation, Automation and Digitisation","In the agricultural sector, robotisation, automation and digitisation of production processes are essential for food security",""],[1,"56","25","Support for Communities in Protected Areas","local communities living in protected areas, including landscape conservation areas (priority landscapes), should be supported in order to strengthen",""],[1,"63","2","Protection of Environmentally Valuable Areas and Ecological Corridors","preservation of environmentally valuable areas and ensured protection of ecological corridors",""],[1,"64","9","Biodiversity and Natural Resources Protection Programme","protecting biodiversity, ecosystems and natural resources",""],[1,"56","25","Responsible Land Use Planning and Development","Responsible land use planning and development reduce the pressure on the natural environment, protect open and undeveloped land, eliminate spatial conflicts and ensure the spatial coherence of natural systems",""]],"6":[[1,"16","12","Integrated Urban Public Transport and Micromobility Infrastructure","public transport infrastructure harmonised with roads for micro-mobility vehicles and pedestrians, particularly in urban areas.",""],[1,"16","12","Low-Cost Public Transport and Logistics Modernisation","Efficient logistics, a convenient and low-cost public transport system, increasingly utilising autonomous vehicles",""],[1,"16","12","Standardised Long-Distance and Regional Transport Network","A coherent and standardised transport network and modern technologies support also long-distance and regional transport.",""],[1,"20","2","Low- and Zero-Emission Public Transport and Micromobility Promotion","Priority was given in all areas to low- and zero-emission public transport, as well as to the use of micromobility vehicles.",""],[1,"21","2","Integrated Accessible Public Transport System","An integrated and accessible public transport system was built and expanded in a manner that allowed it to substantially replace individual transport.",""],[1,"36","8","Transport and Logistics Systems Transformation","It is therefore necessary to change the attitude towards mobility and transform transport and logistics systems.",""],[1,"44","14","Zero-Emission Transport and Logistics Networks","emission transport and logistics networks (e.g. high-speed rail and infrastructure, electromobility for autonomous devices or innovative air mobility)",""],[1,"44","14","Zero-Emission Autonomous Transport Infrastructure Adaptation","extension/adaptation of the traditional infrastructure by adding elements that enable seamless zero-emission and autonomous transport",""],[1,"45","1","Urban and Rural Sustainable Mobility Adaptation","adaptation of urban and rural arrangements to the development of sustainable mobility",""],[1,"45","2","Pedestrian Route Network Development","pedestrian route networkss",""],[1,"45","2","Micromobility Infrastructure Development","infrastructure for micromobility vehicles",""],[1,"55","7","Railway and Public Transport Infrastructure Expansion","expansion of transport infrastructure, especially railways, including public transport,",""],[1,"55","11","Repurposing Ports, River Networks, Airports and Aerodromes","change in the profile of use of certain areas such as ports, river networks, airports and aerodromes",""],[1,"57","6","Transcontinental and Trans-European Transport Links Development","development of transcontinental and trans-European transport links, including seaports",""],[1,"59","4","Low- and Zero-Emission Transport System","a low and zero-emission transport system",""],[1,"59","9","Integrated Environmentally Friendly Transport System Development","develop an integrated, convenient, accessible and environmentally friendly transport system that takes into account specific regional and local circumstances",""],[1,"59","9","Railway Priority and Multimodal Transport Integration","Railway, as the least emission-intensive mode of transport, should be a priority in the state's transport policy, and should be accessible to as many people across Poland as possible, and integrated with other modes of transport.",""],[1,"59","9","Integrated Public Transport Passenger Information System","Complete, up-to-date, integrated and well-organised passenger information should also be provided to facilitate access to public transport.",""],[1,"62","5","Basic Public Transport Standards Programme","ensuring basic standards in public transport",""]],"7":[[1,"21","9","Institutional, Financial and Competence Security Solutions","creating appropriate institutional, financial and competence solutions",""],[1,"21","9","Information Systems and Critical Infrastructure Development","Information systems and the critical infrastructure of the state were developed",""],[1,"21","9","Domestic Industry-Based Army Modernisation","modernisation of the army based on domestic industry and weapon technologies",""],[1,"22","11","Modern Army Creation","Public security was ensured by creating a modern army in accordance with the guidelines set by of security organisations.",""],[1,"22","11","Artificial Intelligence Crime Prevention and Security Monitoring","Artificial intelligence started to be used for crime prevention and security monitoring, including by means of drones and robots patrolling the streets.",""],[1,"47","2","Balanced Military Potential Development","The military potential should be developed evenly",""],[1,"47","4","Armed Forces Training and Technological Modernization","improve the level of training and technological sophistication of the armed forces",""],[1,"47","6","Non-Military Defence Links Development","it is necessary to develop non-military defence links, such as transport, energy, logistic",""],[1,"47","7","Targeted Pro-Defence Training Programme","targeted pro-defence training",""],[1,"47","10","Local Extreme Event Warning and Threat Response Networks","local extreme event warning and threat response networks.",""],[1,"47","12","Humanitarian Aid and Medical Supply Procedures Strengthening","to strengthen procedures for the provision of humanitarian aid, medicinal and medical products and first aid",""],[1,"47","13","Crisis Evacuation and Psychological Support Arrangements","the organisation of evacuation and psychological support for people affected by crisis",""],[1,"20","13","Emergency Management and Strategic Reserves Reform","the emergency management system was reformed and oriented towards the management of food reserves in case of crop failure and energy supply in case of blackouts.",""],[1,"21","17","Emergency Management and Civil Protection Enhancement","enhancements in the emergency management and civil protection system",""],[1,"44","10","Strategic Mineral Deposit Preservation Measure","preservation of strategic mineral deposits as emergency reserves (e.g. by not developing the land above",""],[1,"64","10","National Defence Capability Development","systematically increasing the state's defence capabilities",""],[1,"64","10","Food Security Enhancement Activities","carrying out activities to enhance food security",""]],"8":[[1,"56","7","Long-Term Participatory Spatial Planning","Spatial management should be based on long-term participatory planning",""],[1,"56","22","Spatial Integration in Public Policy Planning","Space and its diversity should be taken into account in the planning and implementation of all public policies.",""],[1,"56","23","Spatial Planning Awareness and Education Programme","education in this area and improved awareness among decision-makers and the public, including children and young people, concerning the perception of space as a rare resource and the necessity to protect and manage it in a reasonable manner",""],[1,"56","23","Private-Social Interest Balancing Mechanism","the development of mechanisms for balancing private and social interests as a sustainable element of the state policy",""],[1,"57","5","Mandatory Integration of Spatial Planning into Development Planning","treating spatial planning as a mandatory part of development planning.",""],[1,"57","7","Urbanisation Control and Planned Spatial Development","It is necessary to achieve urbanisation control by making realistic links to the current and projected population numbers, development needs, access to infrastructure and the protection of valuable natural and agricultural areas.",""],[1,"57","7","Gradual Planned Release of Investment Land","Only then can investment land be released gradually and in a planned manner.",""],[1,"58","4","Development Planning System Organisation and Coordination","It is necessary to continue to organise the development planning system, to strengthen its role and to make it coherent and holistic.",""],[1,"58","4","Development Planning Regulatory Amendment","The efforts that have already been made to amend development planning regulations should be finalised.",""],[1,"58","4","Spatial Analysis Integration in Law-Making and Decision-Making","an analysis of the spatial conditions and effects of specific legal actions and solutions should be integrated into the law-making and decision-making processes.",""],[1,"58","4","Redefinition of Development Planning Actors and Relationships","It is also important to redefine the main actors and objects (at national, regional, functional and local levels) in the development planning system, and rethink how they relate to each other and influence the shaping of space.",""],[1,"58","4","Local Community Engagement in Spatial Development","Effective spatial management should engage local communities in the spatial development process as much as possible.",""],[1,"64","11","Spatial Planning Integration and Coordination Reform","Raise the status of spatial planning and management based on cooperation of local government units (functional approach) in the country's management system",""],[1,"65","1","Sustainable Development Integration into Spatial Policy","deepening the integration of sustainable development principles into spatial development policy",""],[1,"65","2","Integrated Spatial Planning for Environmental Protection","planning, including environmental, landscape, social, economic and functional aspects, so as to minimise spatial conflicts and the negative effects of spatial management on the environment, while supporting the development of local communities",""],[1,"65","2","Innovative Functional Spatial Management Solutions","introducing innovative functional management solutions",""],[1,"65","2","Advanced Technologies for Spatial Planning Decisions","making a greater use of advanced technologies to better understand development patterns and make more effective planning decisions",""],[1,"62","8","Spatial Conservation and Land-Use Planning Strengthening","require strengthening of the spatial conservation, planning and management in order to inter alia preserve agricultural functions and maintain food production",""]],"15":[[1,"13","5","Social Inclusion and Crisis Support Programme","The state strives for social inclusion and integration and supports individuals and families in crisis.",""],[1,"13","5","Social Cohesion and Security Development Programmes","This is facilitated by public institutions and development programmes focused on building and strengthening social cohesion and security, respecting the law and fulfilling the basic needs of every citizen of the country.",""],[1,"19","8","Guaranteed Basic Income Programme","Taxes charged on automation have allowed the introduction of a guaranteed basic income.",""],[1,"19","15","Guaranteed Basic Income Scheme","A guaranteed basic income was introduced, providing income for the part of society that lost their jobs in a highly automated world.",""],[1,"22","3","Guaranteed Basic Income Scheme","the guaranteed basic income, financed from taxes on automation and proceeds from taxes on capital and luxury goods, were also introduced.",""],[1,"19","8","Automation Tax Policy","Taxes charged on automation have allowed the introduction of a guaranteed basic income.",""],[1,"19","15","Automation and Luxury Goods Taxation","Its financing was possible through introduction of additional taxes (taxation of automation and luxury goods, corrective taxes).",""],[1,"31","2","Social Benefit System Employment Incentive Reform","the transformation of the social benefit system so that it does not demotivate people from employment",""],[1,"31","2","Benefits and Care Services System Reform","changes are needed in the system of benefits and care services for those in need of support",""],[1,"31","4","Community-Based Social Services Deinstitutionalisation","for the process of development and de-institutionalisation of social services to engage social economy entities",""],[1,"31","4","Integrated Senior and Family Support Services","to ensure access to the necessary support for seniors and their families",""],[1,"31","5","Inclusive Silver Economy Services Development","it will be important to dynamically develop the services of the silver economy and to ensure that its offer is broadly accessible",""],[1,"31","2","Social Economy Opportunities for Older People","it is necessary to develop and exploit the potential of, among others, the social economy sector where older people can continue to work under conditions that are tailored to their needs",""],[1,"33","10","Social Infrastructure for Older People's Support Services","development of social infrastructure to provide support services and organise activities for older people.",""],[1,"32","9","Social Integration, Sport and Recreation Promotion","encourage social integration, sport, recreation),",""]],"16":[[1,"13","7","Medicine and Medical Services Development","advanced development of medicine and medical services",""],[1,"13","7","Data-Driven Health Promotion and Prevention Programmes","health promotion and prevention data-driven programmes",""],[1,"18","7","Health Promotion and Disease Prevention Programme","enhanced health promotion and disease prevention",""],[1,"21","5","Health Promotion and Disease Prevention Programme","health promotion and disease prevention",""],[1,"42","2","Health Promotion and Disease Prevention Programme","Health promotion and disease prevention",""],[1,"21","3","Workplace Health Promotion and Disease Prevention","health promotion and disease prevention also at the workplace",""],[1,"21","5","Coordinated Healthcare Delivery","coordinated care",""],[1,"21","5","Digital Healthcare Solutions Expansion","greater use of digital solutions, e.g. artificial intelligence and telemedicine, to make healthcare services more efficient and accessible",""],[1,"22","6","Advanced Healthcare Technology Deployment","To improve the healthcare system, successful efforts were made to promote wide use of AI-based solutions, humanoid robots, robot nurses and technological solutions designed to restore mobility for patients with disabilities (e.g. prosthetic limbs and exoskeletons).",""],[1,"22","7","Psychological and Psychiatric Support System Reform","a reform of the psychological and psychiatric support system for people in crisis was undertaken",""],[1,"22","7","Preventive Measures for People in Crisis","preventive measures were introduced",""],[1,"25","10","Physical and Mental Healthcare Reform","reformulate the existing health care (physical and mental)",""],[1,"28","4","Modern Healthcare Development Investment","invest in the development of modern healthcare",""],[1,"29","1","Mental Health and Disease Prevention Support Services","increasing the number of specialists, as well as the development of psychological support services and programs for health promotion and disease prevention",""],[1,"29","1","Youth Adaptation and Well-Being Skills Development","young people are equipped with the skills to adapt to the changing social norms",""],[1,"31","5","Health Care System Transformation","Fundamental changes are therefore needed in, among others, the health care system",""],[1,"32","1","Safe Remote Diagnosis and Treatment Environment","essential to create a safe environment for remote diagnosis and treatment.",""],[1,"32","1","Integrated Mental Health Prevention and Treatment Policy","It is becoming essential to develop effective policies that result in better access to adequate and effective disease prevention, high-quality and affordable psychiatric and psychological healthcare and treatment, and social reintegration programmes.",""],[1,"32","1","Measures to Reduce Availability of Addictive Products","No less important will be measures to reduce the availability of addictive products and substances.",""],[1,"42","7","Technology-Enabled Remote Healthcare Services","In the healthcare system, the opportunities offered by technologies should be harnessed to promote remote pre-diagnostics and disease prevention, perform simple care tasks and educate physicians, other health professionals as well as care and social service providers.",""],[1,"18","7","Remote Health Access and Monitoring System","the widest possible use of technological solutions to facilitate access to medical services and remote health monitoring",""]],"17":[[1,"13","8","Technology-Enabled Personalized Lifelong Learning","Its development is based on new technologies and methods that enable greater personalisation of learning and teaching paths and ongoing verification of knowledge and skills",""],[1,"14","7","Lifelong Digital Competence Development","Building digital competence is an integral part of the education system for all age groups across society – from school children, through students and teachers to IT professionals.",""],[1,"18","7","Future Skills Education System Reform","The growing labour market demand for the skills of the future influenced changes in the educational system",""],[1,"19","14","Comprehensive Education System Reform","The education system, including adult learning, had been reformed with a focus on comprehensiveness, experimentation, individualised learning paths, teamwork and self-assessment and the development of social skills.",""],[1,"19","14","Digital Hygiene Skills Development","opportunities to develop digital hygiene skills were provided.",""],[1,"19","15","Technological Transition Support Programme","It became necessary to provide support to those who found it difficult to grasp the new technological reality.",""],[1,"19","15","Lifelong Learning Development Initiative","Emphasis was also placed on developing a culture of lifelong learning",""],[1,"22","3","Education and Digital Skills Reform","A successful revolution in education has yielded results in the form of creative generations equipped with advanced and specialised digital skills and able to respond to the challenges of the labour market.",""],[1,"22","3","Vocational Retraining Programmes","Workers whose occupations had been replaced by automation were provided with support in the form of e.g. vocational retraining programmes",""],[1,"22","3","Company-Education Partnership Schemes","schemes designed to assist the creation of partnerships between companies developing in new sectors and education/training providers.",""],[1,"25","13","Skill-Oriented and Social Awareness-Raising Education","Skill-oriented and social awareness-raising education",""],[1,"25","14","Primary and Secondary Education System Transformation","It is therefore necessary to fundamentally transform the education system",""],[1,"25","16","Future Skills Education Reform","the education system should put emphasis on equipping learners with key skills and competencies as well as the competencies of the future.",""],[1,"25","17","Emotional Intelligence and Social Competence Education","they need an educational system that is focused on the development of their emotional intelligence and social competence skills",""],[1,"25","18","Civic and Social Engagement Education","The educational system should instil in young people the courage to actively respond to the reality by, among other things, organising themselves or becoming involved in the existing organisations.",""],[1,"26","2","School and Extracurricular Integration Programmes","introduce special school and extracurricular programmes that promote openness and tolerance and support multiculturalism and integration of young people from different backgrounds and countries.",""],[1,"26","3","Talent- and Experimentation-Based Education","The education of children and young people should also be based on the culture of supporting the development of individual talents, aspirations and passions, as well as experimentation (rather than just bridging the deficits).",""],[1,"26","3","Mentor- and Coach-Oriented Teacher Development","Teaching staff should acquire skills similar to those of mentors or coaches, sharing their knowledge and experience",""],[1,"26","4","Educational Task Automation and Learning Personalization","This process of change should be supported by the automation of some of the teachers‘ tasks, e.g. the individualisation of learning, the monitoring of students’ progress or the grading of work.",""],[1,"26","4","Safe Student-Teacher Relationship Development","It will also be important to develop safe student-teacher and student-student relationships based on trust, respect, partnership, communication and cooperation.",""],[1,"26","5","Teacher Adaptation to Contemporary Curriculum Programme","The system should enable teachers to adapt to teaching new content in line with contemporary requirements.",""],[1,"26","5","Innovative Teaching and Learning Quality Improvement","They must have the adequate conditions to enhance the quality and promotion of innovative forms of teaching and learning.",""],[1,"26","5","New Teaching Technologies Adoption","It is important for teachers to use new teaching technologies",""],[1,"26","6","Virtual Reality and E-Learning Integration","technologies such as virtual reality, simulations and e-learning platforms",""],[1,"26","6","Teacher Remuneration and Competency Development","teachers should be adequately remunerated and motivated to continuously improve their competencies and skills.",""],[1,"26","6","Positive-Selection Teacher Recruitment Reform","recruitment should be based on positive selection.",""],[1,"32","7","Multifunctional Educational Space Development","multifunctional space offering greater flexibility of use, e.g. buildings combining educational functions",""],[1,"42","7","Education Digitalisation and Alternative Learning Reform","Therefore, the education system should embrace the aspect of digitalisation, introduce new, alternative and informal ways of learning and provide for a more in-depth and immediate validation and certification of the acquired skills and knowledge.",""],[1,"42","1","Adult Learning and Continuous Skills Development","It is also necessary to strengthen the adult learning culture so that skill development could become a regular element of employer operations and a habit of employees at all stages of their careers.",""],[1,"42","1","Knowledge and Skills Validation and Certification System","a system of validation and certification of knowledge and skills.",""]],"18":[[1,"13","11","Labour Market and Social Service Provision","Labour market institutions and social service providers focus on enabling people to enter, stay in and re-enter the labour market in an increasingly automated and digital environment.",""],[1,"18","7","Voluntary Retirement Extension Measures","measures encouraging the voluntary extension of the retirement age",""],[1,"18","7","Flexible Employment Models for Older Workers","New working models adapted to the needs of people at the retirement age who wish to remain economically active were put in place.",""],[1,"18","7","Deficit-Occupation Specialist Migration Policy","directed the country’s migration policy towards attracting specialists who represent deficit occupations",""],[1,"19","15","Targeted Public Investment for Structural Employment","A system of targeted public investment has also been developed to tackle structural unemployment.",""],[1,"19","15","Economic Diversification in Unemployment-Affected Areas","diversifying economic activity in areas at risk of structural unemployment",""],[1,"19","15","Financial Support for Businesses and Social Economy Actors","providing dedicated financial support to businesses and social economy actors",""],[1,"19","15","Flexible Retirement Options Reform","provided a stimulus for making retirement options more flexible.",""],[1,"21","3","Flexible Work and Care Arrangements","Focus was placed on more extensive use of flexible arrangements - remote working, combining work with childcare and care for persons in need of support",""],[1,"21","3","Labour Market Re-entry Support Programme","programmes supporting re-entry into the labour market",""],[1,"21","3","Workforce Retraining Programme","retraining",""],[1,"22","3","Working Hours Limitation","A limit of working hours ... were also introduced.",""],[1,"22","3","Specialist Retention Incentive Scheme","a system of incentives was put in place to retain specialists (particularly in the field of digital solutions)",""],[1,"25","10","Labour Market Model Reform","reformulate the existing labour market models",""],[1,"31","2","Labour Market Participation and Retention Schemes","New schemes are needed to motivate people to enter the labour market and to support them in staying there for a longer in their lives",""],[1,"31","2","Workforce Skills and Competencies Development Programme","to accompany them in acquiring skills and competencies in a constantly changing working environment",""],[1,"31","2","Egalitarian Economically Active Parenting Promotion","the promotion of egalitarian, economically active parenting in line with the family life phases",""],[1,"42","1","Supportive Career Counselling System","A supportive counselling system should provide for anticipatory actions, rapid response and strengthening of employer-employee-trainer partnerships.",""],[1,"42","1","Domestic Skilled Worker Retention Incentives","Effective incentives must also be put in place to retain workers in the domestic labour market, especially specialists in areas that require high qualifications",""],[1,"42","1","Programmes Supporting Worker Return","programmes providing attractive conditions for return to the country.",""],[1,"42","1","Immigrant Youth Qualifications and Language Programme","special programmes supporting immigrant youth in gaining professional qualifications, learning the Polish language and skills necessary in the labour market.",""]],"19":[[1,"14","2","Migration Policy Implementation Guidelines","The implementation guidelines of the migration policy are included in the labour market, healthcare, education and social integration solutions.",""],[1,"25","10","Migration Policy Reform","reformulate the existing migration policy",""],[1,"21","3","Labour Migration Policy for Shortage Professions","The migration policy has been focused on creating conditions for accepting individuals in professions where there is little interest among",""],[1,"22","8","Selective Migration and Talent Attraction Policy","Based on indicators of talent attractiveness in the context of the Polish economy, the policy was targeted at attracting highly qualified specialists, entrepreneurs and active investors.",""],[1,"22","4","Return Migration Encouragement Initiative","encourage those who live abroad to return to Poland",""],[1,"21","4","Social, Cultural, and Economic Settlement Integration Support","supporting settlement processes aimed at social, cultural, and economic integration, in order to avoid the creation of separate enclaves.",""],[1,"30","1","Migration Integration and Settlement Policy","it is required to have a well-thought-out migration policy that supports the integration and settlement processes of foreign nationals, closely aligned with labor market needs and social expectations",""],[1,"30","2","National Migration Doctrine for Labour Shortages","a socially and politically agreed migration doctrine oriented towards filling the gap caused by the shortage of human resources in key sectors of the economy and in deficit occupations",""],[1,"30","2","Migrant Settlement and Integration Policy Preparation","Public institutions and regulations concerning legalisation of residence, labour market, social security, health care, integration and education system should therefore be adequately prepared to encourage the settlement and integration of migrants closely linked to labor market shortages.",""],[1,"30","2","Immigrant Civic Participation Mechanism","It will be particularly important to create room for the involvement of immigrants in the social and civic life of the country through NGOs, community initiatives and volunteering.",""],[1,"28","4","Youth Return and Flexible Employment Policy","ensuring attractive conditions for returning to the country and promoting flexible forms of employment, such as remote work",""],[1,"30","1","Comprehensive Pro-Natalist and Pro-Family Policy","In addition to a comprehensive pro-natalist and pro-family policy that takes into account various aspects of social, economic and cultural life",""],[1,"25","10","Pro-Natalist and Pro-Family Policy Reform","reformulate the existing pro-natalist and pro-family policies",""]],"20":[[1,"14","5","Technological Capacity Development and Innovation Support","The country systemically supports the development of its existing technological capacities and fosters the creation new ones.",""],[1,"18","7","Science–Business and High-Tech Cooperation Mechanism","the establishment of intensive cooperation with global high-tech corporations",""],[1,"19","12","Startup and Advanced Technology Sector Development","Focus was placed on, among others, the start-up economy and profiling of technology activities (aerospace valley, astronautics, space utilisation).",""],[1,"19","17","Research and Development Centres Investment","Significant resources were allocated to research and development to build strong university and new technology centres.",""],[1,"20","16","Support Programme for Polish Companies and Innovation","Greater support was provided to Polish companies, including those in the innovation sector.",""],[1,"41","3","Innovation Support System Reform","Harnessing opportunities from technological acceleration in socio-economic development should be enabled first and foremost by remodelling of the innovation support and generation system.",""],[1,"41","3","Mission-Oriented Research and Innovation Policy","Innovation support policies should be accompanied by a strategic vision to support mission-oriented research and innovation",""],[1,"41","3","Innovation and Education-Sector Linkage Network","The foundation for change is provided by creating a network of sustainable links between the actors in this system and linking them to the education and science sector.",""],[1,"41","3","Innovation Potential Identification Mechanism","it will be important to identify innovation potentials (e.g. with the use of big data), especially ones that can generate groundbreaking technologies",""],[1,"41","3","Profiled Public and Private Innovation Funding","support them through a profiled policy based both public and private funding (including corporate funding)",""],[1,"41","3","SME Financial and Innovation Support","the SME sector, which is a significant part of the economy and often acts as a bridge between small start-ups and large corporations, will require support. In addition to financial support, it is also important to develop and promote Polish innovations in sectors of the future on international markets",""],[1,"41","3","International Promotion of Polish Future-Sector Innovations","it is also important to develop and promote Polish innovations in sectors of the future on international markets",""],[1,"43","3","Digital Economy Business Model and Policy Reform","It is therefore necessary to change business models and economic policies",""],[1,"43","3","Digital Financial Infrastructure Modernisation and Regulation","modernise the financial infrastructure through relevant regulations and security measures provided by the state",""],[1,"43","5","Balanced Regulation of Modern Technologies","Community efforts should therefore be strengthened to develop balanced regulations concerning modern technologies which, on the one hand, provide a flexible framework for their development and, on the other, prevent their inappropriate evolution.",""],[1,"43","6","Global Corporation Market Monopolisation Countermeasures","develop tools to counter the monopolisation of markets and services by global corporations",""]],"21":[[1,"14","7","Privacy and Cybersecurity Regulatory Standards","The development and use of modern technologies are safeguarded by sustainable regulations and standards aimed to ensure privacy, cybersecurity and the prevention of abuse.",""],[1,"18","7","Virtual World Ethical Conduct Measures","Measures were taken to prevent unethical behaviour in the virtual world.",""],[1,"18","7","Disinformation Countermeasures","Tools were also developed to counteract disinformation",""],[1,"18","7","Digital Privacy Protection Measures","Tools were also developed to ... protect privacy",""],[1,"18","7","Artificial Intelligence and Algorithm Regulation","regulate AI rules, control algorithms and the related legal liability",""],[1,"18","7","Secure Digital Transactions and Communications","to ensure the security of transactions and communication",""],[1,"19","13","Artificial Intelligence Development Regulation","it became crucial to regulate the development of artificial intelligence",""],[1,"32","13","High-Speed Data Transmission Infrastructure Development","a greater emphasis in development planning on the creation of high-speed data transmission",""],[1,"45","7","National Data Transmission Network Infrastructure Development","development of data transmission network infrastructure across the country.",""],[1,"43","6","Online Harm and Cybercrime Counteraction Programme","It is also required to intensify efforts to counteract harmful online activity (hate speech, disinformation, hacking activist, algorithms of trauma), cybercrime and anti-democratic social engineering",""],[1,"43","6","Personal Data and Virtual Organisation Protection","step up actions to protect personal data and organisations operating in the virtual world",""],[1,"43","6","Artificial Intelligence and Algorithm Accountability Regulation","regulate the rules of artificial intelligence, control algorithms and legal liability for them",""],[1,"43","6","Digital Transactions and Privacy Security Measures","ensure the security of transactions and communications, the security of user data and the protection of the right to privacy",""],[1,"43","6","Digital Markets and Services Legislative Response","proactive legislative responses in digital markets and digital services",""],[1,"26","9","New Technology Benefits and Risks Awareness Programme","It is equally important to build awareness of the new technologies both in terms of the benefits they bring and the risks they entail, especially in the area of fundamental rights and democracy",""],[1,"43","5","Technology Education and Public Awareness Efforts","The opportunities and risks associated with technological acceleration also require intensive efforts in the area of education and public awareness",""],[1,"43","3","Public Financial Education Programme","ensure financial education of the public",""]],"22":[[1,"18","7","Climate Change Adaptation and Environmental Protection Measures","increased efforts to improve the environment and prepare solutions for areas vulnerable to the effects of climate change",""],[1,"20","17","National Climate Change Adaptation Strategy","A strategy for adapting the country to climate change has been prepared.",""],[1,"21","17","Climate Adaptation Coordination for Drought and Flood Risk","the efforts of various actors responsible for climate change adaptation management in terms of drought prevention and flood risk minimisation were coordinated",""],[1,"16","8","Blue and Green Infrastructure Development","With blue and green infrastructure systematically replenished and developed, these areas are resilient to climate change and foster human interaction.",""],[1,"18","7","Urban Blue and Green Infrastructure Deployment","the deployment of blue and green infrastructure",""],[1,"21","17","Blue-Green Infrastructure and Catchment Management","the deployment of blue and green infrastructure and catchment management",""],[1,"36","10","River Basin Water Management and Participatory Planning","Therefore, it is necessary to develop water management systems in a river basin (catchment) system and to plan and manage water management problems in a natural system such as hydrological catchments.",""],[1,"37","5","Water Retention Enhancement","It is necessary to increase the level of water retention",""],[1,"37","5","Water Resource Management and Control","It is necessary to ensure stable conditions for the efficient management and control of water resources",""],[1,"37","6","Legal Recognition of Blue and Green Infrastructure","blue and green infrastructure to be recognised as a critical resource by the state legal system",""],[1,"37","6","Blue and Green Infrastructure Development Programme","to be developed systematically, e.g. through river renaturalisation, wetland reclamation and sustainable rainwater management in urbanised areas",""],[1,"15","7","Water-Efficient Technology Deployment","the use of water-efficient technologies in sectors such as agriculture, industry and municipal services management",""],[1,"37","6","Water-Efficient Technology Implementation","It is also necessary to implement modern water-efficient technologies across all sectors of the economy and in municipal service management.",""],[1,"37","6","Universal Municipal and Industrial Sewage Treatment","ensured treatment of all municipal and industrial sewage",""],[1,"44","13","Land Reserve Preservation for Future Energy Needs","preservation of land reserves for future energy needs",""],[1,"44","13","Spatial Adaptation for Low- and Zero-Emission Energy Development","adaptation of developed spatial structures or occupation of new land for the development of low and zero-",""]],"23":[[1,"16","6","Urban Functional Area Organisation and Land-Use Regulation","are organised and regulated, which prevents spatial conflicts and enables rational land planning for the purposes of development, deployment of industrial and service facilities and environmental protection.",""],[1,"16","6","Urban Greening and Nature-Based Water Management","urban greening and proper rainwater and space management policies and the use of nature-based solutions",""],[1,"16","12","Systemic Spatial Planning Reform","A new systemic approach to spatial planning reduced spatial conflicts and also enabled the creation of functional and aesthetically appealing spaces.",""],[1,"18","7","Urban Sprawl Prevention Policy","it was necessary to prevent urban sprawl",""],[1,"18","7","Small and Medium-Sized City Development Package","A package of basic services was introduced, transport accessibility was increased, and the territorial redistribution of income to residents of small and medium-sized towns was improved.",""],[1,"18","7","Local Government Competency and Autonomy Reform","a reform leading to better distribution of competencies and strengthening the independence of the local government",""],[1,"20","16","Local Government Support Financing Mechanisms","Mechanisms were implemented to support local governments, e.g. through local currencies, climate bonds.",""],[1,"20","17","Environmental Subsidies for Local Governments","Mechanisms were put in place to support local communities through e.g. environmental subsidies for local government units",""],[1,"21","2","Low-Quality Space Recycling and Urban Regeneration","areas have been created through recycling of low-quality spaces with underdeveloped socio-economic functions.",""],[1,"21","2","Connections Among Local Centres","Focus was placed on better connections among local centres.",""],[1,"21","15","Compact Multifunctional Local Centres","Poland created compact, multifunctional local centres to meet the",""],[1,"32","10","Adaptive Reuse of Underused Public Spaces","recycling of lesser-used spaces (dormitories, schools in locations affected by demographic decline",""],[1,"33","1","Spatial Accessibility Criteria Reform for Service Provision","a change in the spatial accessibility criteria for services so that they are concentrated in close proximity",""],[1,"33","9","Green Spaces and Recreation Development","development of green spaces with expanded recreational offering and good quality environmental",""],[1,"45","3","Public Space Quality and Functionality Improvement","improved quality and functionality of spaces",""],[1,"45","3","Architectural and Urban Standards Implementation","implementation of new architectural and urban standards",""],[1,"45","4","Land Development and Infrastructure Use Limitation","limitation of land for new development and reduction of unnecessary land infrastructure",""],[1,"45","4","Relocation of Economic Facilities to New Business Areas","potential relocation of economic facilities and occupation of new areas for business activities",""],[1,"19","17","Smart Cities Implementation","the concept of \"smart cities\" was also implemented.",""],[1,"46","10","Local Economic Ties Strengthening Policy","it is necessary to strengthen local economic ties",""]],"24":[[1,"14","5","Global Promotion of Polish Territorial Brands","Their promotion worldwide is one of the key aspects of the state’s foreign policy.",""],[1,"20","16","Supranational Recognition of National Standards","Poland made intensive efforts to ensure supranational recognition of national standards on which domestic solutions and technologies were based",""],[1,"22","9","EU Space and Seabed Resource Coordination Reform Programme","In order to increase the country's energy potential, Poland initiated a programme of reforms within the EU whose main objectives included, among others, coordination of Member State activities in the field of space exploration and the extraction of raw materials from space and the ocean floor.",""],[1,"46","8","International Alliance Cooperation and Participation","active cooperation within the existing international alliances",""],[1,"46","33","Regional Partnership Cooperation Mechanism","cooperation with partners in the immediate environment, e.g. within the Baltic Sea region, is one response to this",""],[1,"46","38","NATO Credibility and Effectiveness Enhancement","fundamental to continue to enhance the credibility and effectiveness of NATO",""],[1,"47","14","Solidarity-Based Development Assistance Policy","it is also necessary for Poland to provide solidarity-based development assistance",""],[1,"47","18","International Climate Adaptation Solidarity Assistance","provide solidarity assistance to poorer countries in their adaptation to climate change",""],[1,"47","20","Asian and Emerging Market Free Trade Partnerships","partnerships and free trade agreements with Asian partners and other emerging markets within European",""],[1,"47","21","Private and Institutional Cooperation Networks","cooperation networks that bring together private investors, national and international institutions and development",""],[1,"47","23","International Cooperation for Space and IT Development","in international cooperation in the fields of space exploration, development of space technologies and the IT sector",""],[1,"18","7","Corporate Partnership in Public Services","a stronger corporate involvement in areas previously dominated by the state",""]],"25":[[1,"48","8","Climate Change Resilience-Building Initiative","build-up of climate change resilience",""],[1,"49","3","Systemic Climate Change Adaptation Approach","It is therefore necessary to introduce a systemic approach to climate change.",""],[1,"48","9","Blue-Green Infrastructure Development","development of blue-green infrastructure will be an important component",""],[1,"49","3","Blue-Green Infrastructure Development","In all types of areas, it will be important to develop a blue-green infrastructure",""],[1,"49","4","Ecosystem Services Restoration Measures","in order to restore ecosystem services",""],[1,"49","4","Urban Flash Flood and Heat Island Reduction","In urbanised areas, it will also be necessary to carry out comprehensive and decisive actions to minimise the occurrence of urban flash floods, heat islands and their effects.",""],[1,"49","4","Coastal Flood and Sea-Level Rise Protection Measures","coastal areas should be subject to strong measures to reduce the effects of rising Baltic Sea water levels and increased frequency of storm floods.",""],[1,"49","5","Natural Ecosystem and Biodiversity Protection Programme","implementation of a comprehensive protection of natural ecosystems and biodiversity, by paying attention to ecosystem services in the management of natural systems",""],[1,"49","5","Ecosystem Restoration Initiative","the restoration of ecosystems",""],[1,"49","5","Climate-Adapted Crop Development","adaptation of crop types",""],[1,"49","5","Agricultural Monitoring and Early Warning Systems","development of monitoring and early warning systems",""],[1,"55","16","Agricultural Land Protection and Climate Adaptation","preservation and protection of agricultural land, adapting it to the effects of climate change",""],[1,"55","19","Flood Risk Area Protection Measures","protection of areas at risk of flooding, including from the sea, urban flash flooding",""],[1,"57","6","Risk-Resilient Spatial Management","Spatial management should take greater account of the prevention and mitigation of risks arising from geopolitical, socio-economic and climate changes",""],[1,"57","6","Soil, Water, and Floodplain Protection Measures","This requires considering a number of factors, including the protection of valuable soils and water resources, blue and green infrastructure, limitation of floodplain development",""],[1,"57","6","Local Climate Change Adaptation Strategies and Plans","Local governments should develop and implement climate change adaptation strategies and plans",""],[1,"58","7","Water Security and Flood Safety Measures","ensuring continued access to water resources in areas at risk of long-term drought and desertification, while ensuring flood safety",""],[1,"64","9","Critical Infrastructure Resilience Programme","ensuring the resilience of critical infrastructures such as energy, transport, ICT",""]],"26":[[1,"51","1","Strategic Autonomy for Critical Goods and Industries","It will be critical to ensure independence of various, including agricultural products, critical raw materials, semiconductors, pharmaceuticals and health products, heavy industry.",""],[1,"50","7","Micro, Small and Medium-Sized Enterprise Support Mechanisms","application of the right support mechanisms can enable the sector to increase the flexibility and resilience of the national economy",""],[1,"50","7","Global Network Participation Support for Polish Companies","it is therefore essential for the state to provide the necessary support to strengthen the participation of companies controlled by Polish citizens in global economic networks and maximise the effectiveness of the Polish business presence in supply chains",""],[1,"51","2","Foreign Investment Attraction and Investment Appeal","strengthen Poland's investment appeal",""],[1,"64","8","Breakthrough Technology Research and Development Investment","investing in research and development of breakthrough technologies (particularly dual-use technologies) within the framework of international alliances to enhance the country's economic",""],[1,"69","10","Research and Innovation Policy","a research and innovation policy aimed at solving global and local challenges.",""]],"27":[[1,"50","6","Domestic Economic Linkages and Resilience Policy","strong local economic links, in addition to global ties, should become an important element of resilience-building policies",""],[1,"50","7","Supply Chain Diversification and Shortening","combined with diversification and shorSng the supply chains of raw materials, resources, goods, value and services",""],[1,"53","8","State Control of Strategic Assets","ensure that the state has control over key tangible (e.g. transport, critical infrastructure, medicines) and intangible assets (e.g. data, information, servers)",""]],"28":[[1,"59","3","Lifelong Competencies Development","creating opportunities for lifelong acquisition of new competencies",""],[1,"65","3","Future Skills Curriculum Reform","teaching curricula emphasise the need to develop skills of the future, support the development of students' talents, develop students’ ability to use modern technologies",""],[1,"65","3","Adult Learning System Development","the adult learning system could enable learners",""],[1,"65","7","Sustainable Adult Learning Culture","building a sustainable adult learning culture",""],[1,"65","5","Strategic Direction of Higher Education Research","directing the research activities of entities within the higher education and science system by defining objectives arising from strategic challenges, while ensuring flexibility for these entities in choosing the most appropriate research methods and technological solutions",""]],"30":[[1,"65","6","Social Market Economy Protection Measures","maintaining the social character of the market economy in the context of technological transformations that may lead to an increased socio-economic",""]],"31":[[1,"62","5","Basic Health Care Standards Programme","ensuring basic standards in health care",""],[1,"62","5","Basic Social Welfare Standards Programme","ensuring basic standards in social welfare",""]],"32":[[1,"51","9","Local Authority Empowerment and Administrative Modernisation","better empower local authorities and modernise their system of functioning in order to enable them to implement a truly integrated development policy",""],[1,"51","9","Modern Local Government Financing Mechanisms","using modern mechanisms to finance their activities",""],[1,"51","10","Joint Local Government Activities for Communities","implementation of joint activities for the benefit of local communities by cooperating local government units.",""],[1,"51","11","Civil Service Ethos Renewal","renewal of the civil service ethos",""],[1,"53","6","Modern Operational Methods for Public Institutions","implement modern operational methods for public institutions to increase their efficiency, effectiveness, flexibility and competitiveness vis-à-vis corporations",""],[1,"64","4","Departmental Cooperation Mechanisms","introduction of departmental cooperation mechanisms",""],[1,"64","5","Local Government Empowerment and Financing Reform","greater empowerment of local government units and modernisation of their financing system to enable them to implement an integrated development policy",""],[1,"59","2","Public Task Coordination and Cooperation Mechanism","basis and opportunities for coordination and real cooperation in the execution of public tasks need to be ensured.",""]],"33":[[1,"52","7","Evidence-Based Law-Making Reform","The law-making process should be more closely based on the principles of sound legislation, which include legislation based on reliable analyses and data, limited use of special purpose laws, legislation based on the principle of the non-retroactivity of laws, adequate vacatio legis and legislation drafted in a clear and understandable manner",""],[1,"52","7","Judicial Staffing Expansion","Furthermore, legislative changes that increase the number of cases in common courts require a corresponding increase in the staffing of the professional groups responsible for hearing them.",""],[1,"52","7","Participatory Law-Making Procedures","It is also necessary to ensure proper law-making procedures that take into account participatory law-making through public consultations.",""],[1,"52","7","Effective Implementation Mechanisms and Tools","Application of this model makes it possible to create good regulations that come into force in sufficient time for institutions and citizens to prepare for change, including the development of effective implementation mechanisms and tools.",""],[1,"52","7","Anti-Corruption Tools","At the same time, well-functioning anti-corruption tools must be created to ensure the stability of democracy, social justice and the integrity of the functioning of the state.",""],[1,"53","3","Participatory Planning and Consensus-Building Mechanism","It is worth utilising this public involvement through harnessing innovative techniques and tools of participatory planning in the spirit of consensus-seeking.",""],[1,"53","3","Civil Society Organisation Support and Enabling Reform","It is therefore necessary, among others, to review and support the conditions for the development of organisations that combat inequality, disinformation and corruption, defend human rights, advocate the rule of law and promote appropriate use of the media, so that they can effectively influence public discourse, political and business decisions, law-making processes and policy implementation.",""],[1,"53","8","Civic Participation and Cooperation Initiative","increase citizens' involvement and willingness to work together to build a better and more stable state",""],[1,"53","6","Corporate Governance and Fair Competition Reform","strive to offset the state's economic dependence on corporations and their influence on the state's decision-making processes, and to ensure the balance between public and private interests and the lawfulness of corporate operations so that they do not harm the society or the environment and preserve fair competition",""],[1,"64","5","Civil Society and Social Partner Engagement","utilisation and enhancement of the potential of civil society for development and organisation of social partners representing the interests of employees and employers, and their wider inclusion in public decision-making processes",""],[1,"64","7","Social Equality and Human Rights Strengthening","strengthening social equality, solidarity and human rights within the established set of state governance values",""]],"34":[[1,"51","2","International Relations Engagement and Cooperation","avoid the insularity of the state through active engagement in international relations (diplomacy, economic, cultural, scientific or political cooperation)",""],[1,"64","7","International Global Challenges Cooperation","active participation in international initiatives and agreements aimed at addressing global challenges",""],[1,"64","9","International Cooperation and Diplomacy Initiative","increasing the state's activity in international cooperation and diplomacy",""],[1,"64","9","European and Transatlantic Alliance Strengthening","strengthening the country's position in European and transatlantic alliances",""],[1,"64","9","Alliance-Building for Threat Response","building other alliances that can enhance the state's ability to respond to potential threats",""],[1,"64","10","European and Global Security Architecture Engagement","European and global work on the future of the EU and transatlantic security architecture in all its dimensions",""],[1,"63","2","Poland-Ukraine Functional and Spatial Cooperation","intensification of functional and spatial links between Poland and Ukraine",""]],"35":[[1,"58","8","Territorial Development Balancing Policy","territorial balancing of development",""],[1,"58","8","Coordinated Spatial Planning Mechanism","coordination of spatial planning and taking e.g. mobility and flows into account",""],[1,"58","9","Metropolitan Area Organisational Capacity Support","In the first place, it is necessary to ensure that metropolitan areas are able to organise",""],[1,"59","2","Polycentric Settlement and Service Access Stabilisation","It will be important to stabilise the polycentric settlement structure in such a way that acceptable access to and standard of services are ensured everywhere.",""],[1,"59","3","Systemic Support for Small and Medium-Sized Cities","It is important to provide systemic support for small and medium-sized cities",""],[1,"59","4","Urban Cooperation and Knowledge Transfer Initiative","strengthening their cooperation with strong urban centres, particularly through economic linkage, transfer of knowledge and information",""],[1,"59","4","Spatial Deconcentration of Public Services","The spatial deconcentration of some of the public services and entities will provide these centres with an additional development boost.",""],[1,"59","7","Multifunctional Local Centres Development","Their extended structures need multifunctional local centres to bring together residents and offer accessible and good-quality public services.",""],[1,"61","4","Inter-City Cooperation and Functional Link Strengthening","the cooperation and strengthening of functional links between cities in order to increase the attractiveness of larger agglomeration areas or entire regions and to attract new residents or investors.",""],[1,"61","8","Rural Renewal Implementation Initiative","An opportunity for the development of these areas lies in a further implementation of the concept of rural renewal",""],[1,"62","4","Knowledge and Innovation Solutions for Rural Development","The application of solutions based on knowledge and innovation with respect for the natural environment and enhancing the importance of natural resources can improve the quality of life, provide high quality services and jobs, which will contribute to solving various rural problems, including depopulation.",""],[1,"62","6","Rural Remote and Mobile Services Development","An opportunity for rural areas lies in the development of a service sector with the use remote and mobile services.",""],[1,"62","6","Rural Tourism and Recreation Development","In areas with unique environmental and landscape values and cultural heritage, opportunities for the development of various forms of tourism and recreation should be exploited.",""]],"36":[[1,"51","9","Digitized Urban Planning and Development Monitoring","monitoring development (e.g., digitized urban planning acts)",""],[1,"59","6","Remote Work Technical Infrastructure","technical conditions that to enable them to work remotely",""],[1,"62","5","Telecommunication Infrastructure Standards Programme","ensuring basic standards in ... telecommunication infrastructure",""],[1,"63","2","Technical Infrastructure and Broadband Network Development","development of technical infrastructure, including broadband networks",""],[1,"65","4","Modern Technology Implementation and Development","implementation of modern technologies in a number of areas important for the functioning of the state and its economy - in particular, education, health, energy transformation, public administration, transport, agriculture, construction, spatial planning, decision-making processes, including the mechanisms of democracy, and also for building the capacity to create modern technologies",""]],"37":[[1,"51","1","Social Economy Development Support","It will also be important to create conditions that support the development of the social economy",""],[1,"65","7","Social Economy Development Support","supporting the development of the social economy",""],[1,"51","1","Territorial Partnership and Community Linkages Initiative","grassroot efforts to build links between local communities and create territorial partnerships as organisational networks",""],[1,"51","1","Local Social Capital and Community Trust Strengthening","It will therefore be important to strengthen the local social capital, local identity and social ties that foster trust, cooperation and exchange of resources among people.",""],[1,"55","5","Brownfield Redevelopment for Small Businesses","developed, low-cost land which is attractive to small-scale businesses, using brownfields,",""],[1,"55","10","Brownfield-Based Production Area Development","new production areas in connection with the location of supply chains in Poland (use of brownfields)",""],[1,"59","2","Social Economy and Cooperative Community Services","In this respect, an important role should be played by the social economy sector, including the cooperative sector, which can meet the key needs of local communities.",""],[1,"53","5","State-Corporate Relationship Framework","In order to prevent corporate domination, the state-corporate relationship needs to be defined properly.",""],[1,"53","8","State-Corporate Cooperation Models","develop specific models of state-corporate cooperation so that corporations contribute to the development of local",""]]}});